    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized explanations, adapt to different learning styles, and help students work through problems step by step. They can be especially helpful for visual learners, offering diagrams and examples. With some refinement, they could even simulate tutoring sessions, making math more accessible and less intimidating."
